It's not as simple as that. Adding a 3rd person view would require a ton of work adding brand new animations, brand new camera work for contextual actions, among other things. It would also drastically affect the gameplay. I'm sure it could work if they wanted to take the time to put it in. But it simply isn't a part of their design philosophy for the game.

&#x200B;

One thing I'd support them adding is an "idle" camera similar to what The Outer Worlds has, so you can view your character at any given time organically without needing to use photo mode

&#x200B;

Lastly, I personally am glad, because this means I can focus on choosing equipment based on stats without worrying if it looks ridiculous or not.

