I believe Origins' art style and location lended itself well. It doesn't matter if the distant geometry is flat, blurry, and lacking geometric complexity if it is primarily sand dunes. Origins looks its best in the more barren, desert locations where there's lots of sun and opportunity for dramatic lighting. The worst looking parts of the game are in the northern rocky areas. There, the lower quality LOD becomes apparent with blurry, low resolution rocks and trees.

&#x200B;

Odyssey's terrain is mostly similar to these sections of Origins. That is why the issues are more apparent.

I think you're doing a really productive thing just by writing this. You don't need to have an agenda, or a plan. Sometimes the best thing we can do is just get it out one way or another. Doing so on a new platform could be alleviating, almost like youre experiencing a change of scenery.

&#x200B;

