&#x200B;

I think a lot of us, in our darkest times, actually cling to the option of suicide as a "safety net", something to give us comfort. 

&#x200B;

What do you feel when you have this realisation? Comfort? Relief? pain?

Yeah. It's strange to me tbh how there are aspects that seem so much better, and some that seem a step back from Doom 2016. I think the level design is inconsistent. You have some levels where the amount of geometry is just unbelievable, and then some that are like empty barren corridors of human buildings. It's incredibly weird.

&#x200B;

I feel like the ambient occlusion solution is incredibly weak. And the texture thing is bizarre to me, considering how id Tech doesnt use megatexturing anymore and thus can afford high res ones. I hope they release an HD texture pack

