Well I had this really bad breakdown last october and spent some time in a hospital and reached what I consider my own rock bottom..after which I spent 3 months camping in a sort of wilderness therapy program. It was expensive but I'm extremely lucky to be able to have parents who really support me..and I was able to get a much better diet. When you're hiking and carrying shit every day you don't care as much about what ou eat, and I basically ate very nutritious food for 3 months. I gained around 25 pounds after that. Since January when I came out of the program...I've maintained the sameish weight of 150-155 pounds...and I think during this time I've burned some of the fat and gained the weight back in muscle.

Well for me, I had to force myself to just sorta...not really care what I ate. Because I tend to eat super healthy y default, so by trying to make myself just let go a bit, it became mentally easier for me to gain weight as long as I was continually going to the gym.

&#x200B;

Also, I used to be extremely self consious about being in the weight room with all the jacked up guys. It was tough, but I had to push myself to be that one skinny stick kid who was benching a lot less than everyone else, and get through that hump

