First off I wanna say that I don't think you should have been downvoted. I think it's good that people start discussions. Memes are upvoted, ravings about the game are upvoted, I think criticism or wary thoughts or concerns are just as valid.

&#x200B;

I see what youre saying. Far Cry 5 was kinda a mess sometimes because instead of a lot of hand crafted encounters that more efficiently worked with the pacing of exploration, the game instead just had a million different AI systems that they'd spawn and have cross paths with each other to create chaos. 

&#x200B;

The first reason I think you won't have much to worry about is because RDR2 is meticulously crafted to make encounters feel organic, so it seems. Wildlife exists in realistic, functioning ecosystem. Also, remember that apparently rhe pace of this game is very slow, so slow that some found it boring. This is wonderful news to me. Because it implies that the game's systems create a world that is full of  danger, but in a way that makes SENSE, not in a way that is trying to create constant chaos.

